(area "semantic" :when "texts or values must be judged by meaning: classified, compared, filtered, ranked, routed or grouped")

(memory "internal/semantic/rules" :when "the agent is about to use a % form, or must choose between a % form and its plain twin"
  "Bare = < member find stay exact: % only where written. Numbers and equal values answer without call, so (%= 2 2.0) free. Same question twice in session = same answer, no second call.
% forms answer yes/no, pick, rate, measure. Rewrite, summarize, extract stay write, summarize, extract. % forms on ids, keys, enum strings: wrong tool, use plain form.
Call can fail: try with fallback where wrong guess is costly. Option, every % call: :timeout ms, default 30000.")

(memory "internal/semantic/judge" :when "the agent must classify, pick a category for, or rate a text or value by meaning and needs the raw probability or score, or set its own threshold"
  "Base, raw numbers for own threshold:

- (%p x \"is a refund request\") gives probability of yes, 0..1.
- (%p-each items \"question\") gives one probability per item, one call.
- (%choose x '(:billing :technical :other)) gives option as written. Option =
  keyword, string, or (option . \"what it means\") . :none value adds \"none of
  these\", returns value when chosen. :min p returns :none value when best
  option less likely than p. :question \"...\" says what is picked.
- (%score x \"urgency\") gives rating 0..4 on very low..very high. Own levels:
(%score x \"urgency\" '(\"can wait\" \"today\" \"right now\")) gives 0..2. Compare
  scores only on same levels.
- (%score-each items \"urgency\" [levels]) gives one score per item, one call.")

(memory "internal/semantic/predicates" :when "the agent must test by meaning whether two texts say the same, which is bigger by some quality, whether a value is a kind of thing, whether facts are enough to act, or whether a text mentions something; or an exact test just missed a match it should have caught"
  "Predicates, t or nil, take :min p (default 0.5) :

- (%= \"Hi there!\" \"Hello!\") , (%/= a b) ; :context \"politeness\" compares only by that.
- (%< \"a cat\" \"a horse\" :by \"size\") , %> %<= %>= ; numbers compare exact.
- (%is-a row \"person data\")
- (%enough? facts \"to book the flight\") , nil = ask user, do not guess.
- (%string-contains? mail \"a refund\") , %string-prefix? %string-suffix? ;
  literal match answers without call.")

(memory "internal/semantic/lists" :when "the agent holds a list of texts or records and must find, filter, remove, count, test, sort or take the best of them by meaning"
  "Lists, whole list in one call:

- (%member \"a refund\" topics) gives tail like member.
- (%find \"a pet\" animals) gives element or nil ; (%position \"a pet\" animals) gives index or nil.
- (%filter \"engineers\" staff) , (%remove-if \"spam\" mails) , (%count-if \"negative\" reviews)
- (%some \"urgent\" tickets) , (%every \"in English\" msgs)
- (%sort tickets :by \"urgency\" :desc t) , (%max offers :by \"value for money\") , %min.
  :levels '(...) for own rubric.")

(memory "internal/semantic/branching" :when "the agent must route a text or value to one of several actions depending on what it means, such as handling a ticket by its kind"
  "Branching, one call picks clause, body runs as plain Lisp:

(%cond ticket
  (\"asks for a refund\" (refund ticket))
  (\"reports a bug\" (file-bug ticket))
  (t (escalate ticket)))

(%case weather (:hot (stay-in)) (:mild (walk)) (t (check-again)))

t clause runs when nothing fits; no t clause gives nil.")

(memory "internal/semantic/embedding" :when "the agent must measure how close texts are in meaning, drop near-duplicates, group similar items, rank by closeness to a query, spot outliers, or classify from examples"
  "Meaning as numbers:

- (%embed x) gives vector, list of numbers.
- (%similarity a b) gives cosine, near 1 = same meaning. Raw number for own threshold.
- (%remove-duplicates xs) drops element meaning same as earlier one, first kept;
  :min similarity, default 0.8.
- (%cluster xs) gives groups, list of lists, list order kept; :min similarity,
  default 0.47. Raise :min for tighter groups.
- (%sort xs :near q) orders by meaning distance from q, closest first:
(head (%sort issues :near \"billing problems\") 5) = five closest.
(%min xs :near q) = closest, (%max xs :near q) = farthest.
- (%similarity-each x items) gives one similarity per item, one call.
- (%outliers xs) gives elements nothing else in xs is close to; :min
  similarity, default 0.47.
- (%choose x options :examples '((:billing \"I was charged twice\")
    (:technical \"app crashes\"))) picks option with nearest example, no
  probability call; :min = least similarity.")
